      "id": 1,
      "text": "Franklin became the county seat of Robertson County in 1879, solidifying its role in local governance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franklin%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Originally named Morgan after a railway official, the town changed its name to Franklin when another post office claimed the original name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/franklin-tx-robertson-county",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Situated near the county’s geographic center, Franklin sits on an upland prairie drained by three creeks: Touchstone, South Mineral, and Cedar.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franklin%2C_Texas",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Franklin is the county seat of Robertson County, Texas, and lies within the Brazos Valley on the cusp of East and Central Texas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franklin%2C_Texas",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town hosts the Pridgeon Community Center and Visitor Center, the historic Robertson County Courthouse, a Carnegie Library, and Franklin Cemetery.",
